# ── 20. Career Mode's files agree with each other (added 2026-10-17) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Why: career/ is the design of the gamification system, kept as .toml files Amir edits by hand (Amir, 2026-10-17: "files i can
# then change, adjust"). scripts/check_career.py reads all seven and blocks a reward with no meaning, a fact nobody defined, a
# mission with its own fixed XP (GAME-7), a title that does not exist, tiers out of order, or gold. Its coverage warnings never
# block. test_check_career.py proves the checker still fails on each fault, and runs only when the checker or its test changes.
# Since phase 1 (stage66, 2026-10-17) Career Mode scores habits with Proof's own numbers until rulebook.toml's [switch] catalogue
# is turned on (phase 3; [shadow] until phase 2), and the checker holds them equal to supabase/xp_rules_snapshot.json: a change to
